  "name": "Question 31",
  "problem": "|  | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ |\n\nCompute $P(X=1\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y<2)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above.",
  "worked_solution": "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=1\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y<2) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(0,1),(1,1),(1,2),(2,1)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(0,1))+P((X,Y)=(1,1)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(1,2))+P((X,Y)=(2,1)) \\\\  & =f(0,1)+f(1,1)+f(1,2)+f(2,1) \\\\  & =0.1+0.25+0.1+0.25 \\\\  & =0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
